      "content": "those are good starting points. to make them more specific for the survey, could you give me some actual examples of how those 'social strategies' might manifest in a way that's recognizable? like, what kind of specific verbal or non-verbal cues would we be looking for in these high-risk urban settings? for instance, when it comes to 'navigating authority' or 'conflict,' are there certain ways of communicating—maybe regarding tone, slang, or even more aggressive physical posture—that are characteristic of these specific demographic groups? i just want to make sure the researcher can actually identify the behavior in the participants.",
